From 1ee0db2b7b662508c0ef35a56835f976b5a6c692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:34:03 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 37/43] mm: vmscan: write back dirty swap-cache folios

Since shmem_writepage() and swap_writepage() were removed, pageout()
writes only folios in a shmem mapping or anonymous folios and keeps
activating everything else.  A shmem folio that swapin readahead, such
as MADV_WILLNEED, left only in the swap cache matches neither: its
mapping is the swap address space.  zswap marks every folio it loads
into the swap cache dirty, so under memcg pressure such folios can be
neither cleaned nor freed, and reclaim loops until the cgroup OOMs with
nothing to kill.

Send dirty swap-cache folios to swap_writeout(), which writeout()
already selects for every non-shmem mapping.
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index 95b1179a..7e2cac3a 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -716,7 +716,14 @@ static pageout_t pageout(struct folio *folio, struct address_space *mapping,
 		return PAGE_KEEP;
 	}
 
-	if (!shmem_mapping(mapping) && !folio_test_anon(folio))
+	/*
+	 * A shmem folio that swapin readahead left only in the swap cache
+	 * has the swap address space as its mapping and is not anonymous.
+	 * It can still be dirty (zswap dirties every folio it loads into
+	 * the swap cache), and swap_writeout() is its only writeback path.
+	 */
+	if (!shmem_mapping(mapping) && !folio_test_anon(folio) &&
+	    !folio_test_swapcache(folio))
 		return PAGE_ACTIVATE;
 	if (!folio_clear_dirty_for_io(folio))
 		return PAGE_CLEAN;
